From: RG35XX Java Platform
Task: RGJ-B6-002..006 / RGJ-RC1-011R / RGJ-RC1-011BV
Subject: [PATCH] Libretro: bind RG35XX lifecycle and headless boot baseline

This executable diff owns the Java-side lifecycle boundaries that are already
present in pinned Libretro.java. Native process teardown and EOF/platformShutdown
remain owned by 0017 so the same parser tail is not patched twice.

RGJ-RC1-011BV also establishes the minimal RG35XX AWT boot baseline. The real
device reached JamVM but GNU Classpath selected GtkToolkit and failed on missing
libgtkpeer.so before MobilePlatform/MIDlet startup. Libretro is headless by
definition on RG35XX, so main() selects GNU Classpath HeadlessToolkit before the
Libretro constructor creates MobilePlatform/PlatformFont. This does not add GTK,
does not alter desktop launchers, and remains reversible if the stock device
Classpath cannot provide a usable headless peer.

The source is pinned exactly, so this revision uses insertion-only hunks at the
verified line boundaries to remove GNU patch fuzz/context ambiguity.

--- a/src/org/recompile/freej2me/Libretro.java
+++ b/src/org/recompile/freej2me/Libretro.java
@@ -20,0 +21,1 @@
+import org.recompile.mobile.RG35XXLifecycle;
@@ -52,6 +53,10 @@
 	public static void main(String args[])
 	{
+		/* RG35XX/libretro is a headless target. Select the Classpath headless
+		 * peer before MobilePlatform -> PlatformFont can initialize AWT. */
+		System.setProperty("awt.toolkit", "gnu.java.awt.peer.headless.HeadlessToolkit");
+
 		Mobile.clearOldLog();
 		Libretro app = new Libretro(args);
 	}
@@ -87,0 +93,3 @@
+
+		/* Process-lifetime target services attach after MobilePlatform exists. */
+		RG35XXLifecycle.platformStart();
@@ -176,0 +185,3 @@
+								/* Flush/reset the previous game before MobilePlatform.load()
+								 * replaces loader/suite context. */
+								RG35XXLifecycle.beforeGameLoad();
@@ -178,0 +190,1 @@
+									RG35XXLifecycle.afterGameLoad();
@@ -192,0 +205,1 @@
+									RG35XXLifecycle.gameLoadFailed();
